1
00:06:38,571 --> 00:06:44,571
One day. One planet. Infinite wonder.

2
00:13:17,142 --> 00:13:23,142
Earth: One Amazing Day is a documentary, family,
adventure film directed by Lixin Fan.

3
00:19:55,714 --> 00:20:01,714
An astonishing journey revealing the awesome power of the natural world.

4
00:26:34,285 --> 00:26:40,285
Over the course of one single day, we track the sun from the highest
mountains to the remotest islands to exotic jungles.

5
00:33:12,857 --> 00:33:18,857
Narrator (voice), played by Robert Redford.

6
00:39:51,428 --> 00:39:57,428
Narrator (voice), played by Jackie Chan.

7
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:36,000
Narrator (voice), played by Lee Je-hoon.

8
00:53:08,571 --> 00:53:14,571
The Day the Earth Stood Still is a 2008 American science fiction film serving as a remake of the 1951 film of
the same name, which, in turn, was based on the 1940 short story "Farewell to the Master".

9
00:59:47,142 --> 00:59:53,142
Directed by Scott Derrickson from a screenplay by David Scarpa, it stars Keanu Reeves as Klaatu, an alien sent to try to change human behavior in an effort to save Earth from
environmental degradation; this version replaces the Cold War–era theme of potential nuclear warfare with the contemporary issue of negative human impact on the environment.

10
01:06:25,714 --> 01:06:31,714
It co-stars Jennifer Connelly, Jaden Smith, John
Cleese, Jon Hamm, and Kathy Bates.

11
01:13:04,285 --> 01:13:10,285
The Day the Earth Stood Still was originally scheduled for release on May 9, 2008, but was released on a
roll-out schedule beginning December 12, 2008, screening in both conventional and IMAX theaters.

12
01:19:42,857 --> 01:19:48,857
It was met with generally negative reviews from critics but was a
financial success, grossing over $233 million worldwide.

13
01:26:21,428 --> 01:26:27,428
The film explores themes of earth, animals, nature.
